NUM-44: compare month/day dates with the current date in the same 365-day calendar

OptionsHandler (SWEEP_START/SWEEP_END) and Controls (DAYOFYEAR = MM/DD)
store month/day dates as their day of year in a non-leap year, like legacy
SWMM, but compared them with datetime::dayOfYear() of the current date,
which is one higher from Mar 1 on in a leap year. Add
datetime::dayOfYear365() (Feb 29 = 59.5) and use it for SIM_DAYOFYEAR and
for the sweeping season in SWMMEngine and SurfaceQuality2D. Same change as
NUM-44_swmm530.patch; non-leap years are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply NUM-44_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/2d/quality/SurfaceQuality2D.cpp b/src/engine/2d/quality/SurfaceQuality2D.cpp
index b778c8b..f452ccf 100644
--- a/src/engine/2d/quality/SurfaceQuality2D.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/2d/quality/SurfaceQuality2D.cpp
@@ -500,7 +500,7 @@ void SurfaceQuality2D::step(const SimulationContext& ctx, const MeshData& mesh,
     const double q_to_display = si_ ? 1000.0 * 3600.0 : 39.3700787 * 3600.0;   // m/s → mm/hr | in/hr
     const double ucf_flow     = ucf::UCF(ucf::FLOW, ctx.options);                 // cfs → display flow
     // sweeping season (the A7 block's rule)
-    const int sweep_doy = datetime::dayOfYear(abs_time);
+    const double sweep_doy = datetime::dayOfYear365(abs_time);
     const int ss = ctx.options.sweep_start, se = ctx.options.sweep_end;
     const bool in_season = (ss <= se) ? (sweep_doy >= ss && sweep_doy <= se)
                                       : (sweep_doy >= ss || sweep_doy <= se);
